hifiberry-squeezelite (2.0.0.1564) stable; urgency=medium

  * postinst: do not restart config-server. When the web interface installs
    an extension, config-server is the process running apt and it holds the
    install job the UI polls in memory, so restarting from the postinst --
    which runs during dpkg's configure step, mid-install -- destroyed that
    job. The package installed correctly (apt runs under systemd-run and
    survives) but the UI reported the install as lost. The restart was also
    unnecessary: configurator re-reads conf.d in place after every extension
    install.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 18:30:00 +0000

hifiberry-squeezelite (2.0.0.1563) stable; urgency=medium

  * Publish as a HiFiBerry extension: declare the XB-Extension metadata so
    the package appears in the web interface's extension catalog. Removed
    from the hbos-full bundle, which now installs it on demand instead.
  * Ship the WebUI player descriptor and its icon
    (/etc/hifiberry/players.d/squeezelite.json). These were never packaged
    -- they existed only as hand-placed files on individual devices, so the
    player appeared in the WebUI there and nowhere else. As an extension
    that gap would be fatal: installing it would register no player at all.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 11:00:00 +0000

